     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><div>Dear RStan users,</div><div><br></div><div>I am implementing an Emax model to model the logit of probability of success for binary-outcome data. During sampling, the following exception was thrown out frequently.</div><blockquote style=\"margin-right:0px\" dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Informational</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Message</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">The</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> current </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Metropolis</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> proposal </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">is</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> about to be rejected because of the following issue</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"></span></div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Exception</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> thrown at line </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">244</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> stan</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">::</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">math</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">::</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">binomial_logit_log</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Probability</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> parameter</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">is</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">nan</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> but must be finite</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">!</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">If</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">this</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> warning occurs sporadically</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> such </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">as</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">for</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> highly constrained variable types like covariance matrices</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">then</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> the sampler </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">is</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> fine</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"></span></div><div>but <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">if</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">this</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> warning occurs often </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">then</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> your model may be either severely ill</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">conditioned </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">or</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> misspecified</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span></div></span></code></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>The related code snippet is as follows (the actual model/code is really messy so I just pick out the related portion).</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">data {<br>...<br>}<br><br>parameters </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">{</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> logphiA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  real</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">lower</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> sigmaA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  <br>  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">// npara_DLT = 4: alpha_beta_DLT = (e0, emax, log_hill, log_ec50);</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">npara_DLT</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> alpha_beta_DLT</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> <br>  <br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">  ...<br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">}</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br>model </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">{</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  logphiA </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> multi_normal</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mulogphiA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Sigma_logphiA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">);</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  sigmaA </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> lognormal</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">mulogsigmaA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> sigma_logsigmaA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">);</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  alpha_beta_DLT </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> multi_normal</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">muDLT</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">SigmaDLT</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">);</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">// data likelihood: logX and Y: 9-by-1 vector;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  logX </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">logphiA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> exp</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">logphiA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">])</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> rescale_log_dA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> sqrt_vec</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">pow</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">sigmaA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">./</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> NPK</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">));</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  Y </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> gamma</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">((</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">NPK </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">/</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2.0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">/</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> pow</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">sigmaA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)));</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">NdA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> logit_pi_adm_A</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  vector</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">NdA</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> logit_pi_adm_A_corrected</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  <br>  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">// Emax model: logit_prob = e0 + emax * (exp(log_hill * (logX - log_EC50) / (1 + exp(log_hill * (logX - log_EC50)))))</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  logit_pi_adm_A </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> alpha_beta_DLT</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> alpha_beta_DLT</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">exp</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">alpha_beta_DLT</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">3</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">logX</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> alpha_beta_DLT</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">4</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]))</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">./</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> exp</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">alpha_beta_DLT</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">3</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">logX </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> alpha_beta_DLT</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">4</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]))));</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>  <br>  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">// print(logit_pi_adm_A);</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br> <br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">  // the following is just to restrict logit_prob within (-20, 20)<br>  logit_pi_adm_A_corrected </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> logit_pi_adm_A </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> step_vec</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">logit_crit </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> logit_pi_adm_A</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">logit_crit </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> logit_pi_adm_A</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> step_vec</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">logit_pi_adm_A </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> logit_crit</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">logit_crit </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> logit_pi_adm_A</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">);</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><font color=\"#0b5394\">  DLT </font></span><font color=\"#ff0000\"><font color=\"#00ff00\"><font color=\"#990000\"><font color=\"#0b5394\"><span>~</span><span> binomial_logit</span><span>(</span><span>NDLT</span><span>,</span><span> logit_pi_adm_A_corrected</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">); // This is Line 244</span></font></font></font></font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br>  ...<br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">}</span></div></code></div><div><br><br></div><div><div>What strange to me is that, if I print out &quot;<font color=\"#880000\">logit_pi_adm_A</font>&quot; for debugging, there were no NaN values at all (at least for 200 iterations). So I am not sure why there are such exceptions during sampling. I assume this issue affects the convergence:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Warning</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> messages</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">There</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> were </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">3928</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> divergent transitions after warmup</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Increasing</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> adapt_delta above </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0.8</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> may help</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">There</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> were </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">10009</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> transitions after warmup that exceeded the maximum treedepth</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Increase</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> max_treedepth above </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">10.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">3</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Examine</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> the pairs</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">()</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> plot to diagnose sampling problems</span></div></code></div><br></div><div>I&#39;d really appreciate any comments. Thank you very much!</div><div><br></div><div>Yaohui</div></div></div>"
    ]
